---
import '@/styles/global.css';
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="zh-CN" class="dark">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Dragger - Playground</title>
</head>
<body class="h-screen bg-background text-foreground overflow-hidden">
    <div class="h-full flex flex-col">
        <header class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 bg-card">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                <a href="/" class="text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground transition-colors">← Back</a>
                <span class="text-sm font-medium">Dragger Playground</span>
            </div>
            <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">Drag blocks to rearrange</span>
        </header>
        <main class="flex-1 overflow-auto">
            <div id="editor" class="h-full w-full"></div>
        </main>
    </div>

    <script>
        import { ink } from 'ink-mde';

        const sampleDoc = `# Dragger Playground

Welcome! This is a full-screen editor with drag & drop enabled. Grab any block by its left-edge handle and move it.

## Getting Started

Hover the left margin of any block to reveal the drag handle (⠿). Click and hold, then drag up or down to rearrange.

## Block Types

You can drag all kinds of blocks:

### Headings

Headings of any level are draggable. Try moving this H3 above the H2.

### Lists

- Bullet list item one
- Bullet list item two
- Bullet list item three

1. Ordered item alpha
2. Ordered item beta
3. Ordered item gamma

### Code Blocks

\`\`\`typescript
interface DragConfig {
    autoScrollEdgeZone: number;
    autoScrollMaxSpeed: number;
    mobileDragLongPress: number;
}
\`\`\`

### Blockquotes

> "The best way to predict the future is to invent it."
> — Alan Kay

> "Simplicity is the ultimate sophistication."
> — Leonardo da Vinci

## Multi-block Selection

Long-press a handle to enter multi-block selection mode. Then click additional handles to select more blocks and move them all together.

## Cross-file Drag

In Obsidian, you can drag blocks between open editors, into internal links, or onto files in the explorer.

---

That's it! Try rearranging this document to see how it feels.
`;

        ink(document.getElementById('editor')!, {
            doc: sampleDoc,
            interface: {
                appearance: 'dark',
                toolbar: true,
                attribution: false,
            },
        });
    </script>
    <style is:global>
        #editor .ink-mde { height: 100%; display: flex; flex-direction: column; border: none; border-radius: 0; }
        #editor .ink-mde .cm-editor { flex: 1; }
        #editor .ink-mde .cm-editor.cm-focused { outline: none; }
        #editor .ink-mde .ink-mde-toolbar { border: none; }
        #editor .ink-mde .cm-scroller { overflow: auto; }
        #editor .ink-mde .cm-content { max-width: 48rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.5rem; }
        #editor .ink-mde .cm-gutters { display: none; }

        /* Scrollbar */
        #editor *  {
            scrollbar-width: thin;
            scrollbar-color: oklch(0.3 0 0) transparent;
        }
        #editor *::-webkit-scrollbar { width: 8px; }
        #editor *::-webkit-scrollbar-track { background: transparent; }
        #editor *::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb { background: oklch(0.25 0 0); border-radius: 4px; border: 2px solid transparent; background-clip: padding-box; }
        #editor *::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover { background: oklch(0.35 0 0); border: 2px solid transparent; background-clip: padding-box; }
    </style>
</body>
</html>
